     "text": "{\"count\": 3, \"rationale\": \"Three blocks are enough: block h1_0:access, h2_2:pivot and h1_1:pivot. h3_0 (an AND step) then loses its parent h1_0. h3_1 loses both of its parents, h2_2 and h1_0. h3_2 loses all three of its parents, h1_0, h1_1 and h2_2. So crown:obtain cannot be reached. Two blocks are not enough. h1_1 is reachable directly from the footholds, so any working set must block either h1_1 or h3_2. With the second block, h3_1 must also be stopped, and that takes either h3_1 itself or two blocks (h1_0 plus h2_2 or h1_2). If the second block is h3_1, then either h1_0 still reaches h3_2 (when h1_1 was chosen) or h3_0 stays reachable through h1_2 and h1_0 (when h3_2 was chosen). So no pair of blocks works, and the minimum is 3.\"}"
